{
  "abstract": "We study the intersection of the order-three elliptic sextuple construction of Dujella–Kazalicki–Mikić–Szikszai with Gibbs's regular-sextuple equation. For a full distinct nonzero rational seed triple, we derive the orbit cubic and factor the six-variable Gibbs polynomial. One component contains a zero orbit entry; the only nonzero candidate has explicit parameter $V_0$. When this cubic splits over $mathbb{Q}$ and collision conditions are avoided, all twelve missing square roots are automatic: a $3$-isogeny gives rational orbit points, chord identities give adjacent pair roots, and a row-product identity recovers each individual cross edge. We express the remaining split as a cube in a norm-one torus over $mathbb{Q}(\\sqrt{-3})$, and combine the seed and cube lifts into the symmetric source $R(p)R(v)=R(u)^2$, where $R(T)=T(T^2-9)/(T^2-1)$. An exact height-$256$ pilot found no nonboundary rational source point; this is finite evidence, not a nonexistence proof. We also prove that a Möbius ruling coordinate can only lie on a projective or pole boundary. No new sextuple or septuple is claimed. The result gives a reusable complete-lift criterion and separates quotient, descent, and seventh-entry mate conditions.",
